 inflation to the 2% target. The labor market remains resilient, with unemployment at 4.1% in July, supporting the view that the current 3.50-3.75% target range is not yet sufficiently restrictive. Upcoming September PCE and employment data, along with the next FOMC decision, remain key swing factors for near-term repricing.","context_requires_regen":true,"context_updated_at":"2026-08-21T23:01:35.851Z"},"version":"v1"}]
